\description{
Analyzes prioritized (hierarchically ordered) composite endpoints using the
win ratio, win odds, and net benefit. Every subject in the index group is
compared with every subject in the reference group. Each pair is classified
as a win, loss, or tie by examining endpoints in order of clinical priority
(e.g. death, then hospitalization, then a continuous biomarker): the first
endpoint that can distinguish the pair decides it. The win ratio is the
number of wins divided by the number of losses. Confidence intervals use
the Dong et al. (2016) analytic variance of the log win ratio; a
subject-level bootstrap option is also provided. This complements
hazard-ratio and RMST analyses when outcomes of differing severity must be
combined and ranked.
}
